Subject: [PATCH] usb/xhci: report each successful IOC in a chained transfer

Do not suppress a final IOC after an intermediate successful IOC. Retain
the existing short/error handling. Intel xHCI sections 4.10.1 and 4.11.7.

--- a/hw/usb/hcd-xhci.c
+++ b/hw/usb/hcd-xhci.c
@@ -1550,7 +1550,11 @@
                 edtla = 0;
             }
             xhci_event(xhci, &event, TRB_INTR(*trb));
-            reported = 1;
+            /* A successful intermediate IOC does not terminate event reporting:
+             * another IOC in the same chained transfer needs its own event.
+             * Keep the existing terminal-short suppression and error return.
+             */
+            reported = shortpkt;
             if (xfer->status != CC_SUCCESS) {
                 return;
             }
